WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:03.980
After setting out to establish
a route to Shiganshina,

00:03.980 --> 00:09.480
the Scout Regiment encountered
an intelligent, female Titan.

00:16.860 --> 00:19.660
As soldier after soldier fell,

00:19.660 --> 00:23.070
the regiment rushed
into a forest of giant trees,

00:23.070 --> 00:25.670
much to everyone's puzzlement.

00:25.670 --> 00:29.900
Who can possibly stop it,
if not the Levi Squad?!

00:31.510 --> 00:33.410
Another one's dead!

00:33.410 --> 00:35.710
We could've saved him, too!

00:36.980 --> 00:38.380
Choose.

00:38.380 --> 00:40.380
Will you trust yourself,

00:40.380 --> 00:44.910
or me, these guys,
and the entire Scout Regiment?

00:46.720 --> 00:49.390
I'll go with you!

00:54.730 --> 00:56.720
Fire!

01:04.940 --> 01:06.540
You don't mean?!

01:06.540 --> 01:10.010
They're going to take that Titan alive?!

01:10.010 --> 01:13.920
What do you think of that, Eren?!
We caught that Titan!

01:13.920 --> 01:18.050
This is the might of the Scout Regiment!
Don't underrate us, you idiot!

01:18.050 --> 01:19.890
Now do you see?!

01:21.190 --> 01:22.590
Yes!

01:25.360 --> 01:28.030
It looks like she's stopped.

01:28.030 --> 01:30.070
We can't drop our guard yet.

01:30.070 --> 01:34.240
I'm just impressed you
managed to lead her to this spot.

01:34.240 --> 01:37.740
The credit goes to the rear squad
members who gave their lives fighting her.

01:37.740 --> 01:40.110
They bought us time.

01:40.110 --> 01:42.580
It would've been impossible otherwise.

01:42.580 --> 01:44.110
Is that so?

01:44.110 --> 01:45.550
Yes.

01:46.480 --> 01:48.490
Thanks to them...

01:48.490 --> 01:52.890
...we get to see who's
inside this one's nape.

01:52.890 --> 01:56.450
Let's just hope they're not
wetting themself inside there...

02:01.620 --> 02:02.980
Oh, my friend!

02:02.980 --> 02:05.500
This is a victory for us!

02:05.560 --> 02:08.660
Our fame starts here!

02:08.700 --> 02:09.760
Oh, my friend!

02:09.760 --> 02:14.960
Let us celebrate this victory for the next battle!

02:29.600 --> 02:35.140
"I died for naught"
I won't let it end like that for you

02:35.140 --> 02:40.400
until I am the last one standing

02:40.400 --> 02:43.380
The enemy is cruel... We will kill...

02:43.380 --> 02:46.420
The enemy is colossal... We will jump...

02:46.420 --> 02:50.060
In our hands we hold blades of glory

02:50.060 --> 02:52.340
and sing in the name of victory

02:52.340 --> 02:56.980
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

02:58.300 --> 03:04.420
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

03:04.440 --> 03:08.960
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

03:10.540 --> 03:12.860
and soar through the sky

03:12.920 --> 03:17.120
with our wings of freedom

03:30.880 --> 03:35.880
Erwin Smith: The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 4

03:42.730 --> 03:44.170
An Abnormal...

03:44.170 --> 03:47.660
Or is it like the Colossal Titan?

03:48.870 --> 03:50.710
Wait, did Commander Erwin actually...?

03:50.710 --> 03:53.280
Hey! Quit spacin' out!

03:53.280 --> 03:54.280
Eren!

03:54.280 --> 03:57.880
You can think later!
We need to get further ahead!

03:57.880 --> 03:59.280
Right!

04:04.950 --> 04:06.890
Wait, Levi.

04:06.890 --> 04:08.730
We need to be extra cautious.

04:08.730 --> 04:10.290
Waves 2 and 3!

04:10.290 --> 04:12.360
Fire!

04:12.360 --> 04:14.590
Use the reserves too!

04:32.450 --> 04:34.950
Umm, they're starting to climb up...

04:34.950 --> 04:36.150
Indeed.

04:36.150 --> 04:40.290
If they make it up this far,
perhaps I'll step out of the way.

04:40.290 --> 04:41.490
Although...

04:41.490 --> 04:45.500
I suspect we'll soon be given
orders to withdraw anyway.

04:45.500 --> 04:50.570
Does it have something to do
with those explosions inside the forest?

04:50.570 --> 04:52.160
I don't know.

04:54.800 --> 04:56.140
Mikasa...

04:56.140 --> 04:58.610
What do you think those sounds are?

04:58.610 --> 05:01.840
Are cannons being
fired inside the forest?

05:04.410 --> 05:07.820
I didn't see them bring
any cannons in, though...

05:07.820 --> 05:10.790
What's with all this damn noise?

05:10.790 --> 05:12.290
Hey, Mr. Bertholdt.

05:12.290 --> 05:14.620
Do you know which way Christa went?

05:14.620 --> 05:16.960
Sorry. I don't.

05:16.960 --> 05:19.360
Nothing makes sense anymore.

05:19.360 --> 05:21.800
What are we even doing now, and why?

05:21.800 --> 05:23.360
I wanna go home...

05:25.800 --> 05:28.360
- Let's move away, Armin!
- Right!

05:35.610 --> 05:38.310
Looks like the bastard's
gotten the hang of it.

05:38.310 --> 05:40.820
It's gotten better and
better at tree-climbing!

05:40.820 --> 05:44.490
The scary thing is that
this means they can learn.

05:44.490 --> 05:47.190
Although I'm sure it's
different for each Titan too.

05:47.190 --> 05:48.630
Armin.

05:48.630 --> 05:51.460
They seem to be up to
something inside the forest,

05:51.460 --> 05:54.460
and I think I've
figured out what it is.

05:54.460 --> 05:57.130
They lured that female Titan here

05:57.130 --> 05:58.730
to capture her.

06:00.340 --> 06:06.010
Or, more precisely,
to capture the human inside.

06:06.010 --> 06:08.480
That was Commander Erwin's goal...

06:09.210 --> 06:11.150
...from the very start.

06:11.150 --> 06:13.480
Wasn't it?!

06:13.480 --> 06:18.420
Still, I can understand keeping
it from us rookies, but you guys too?!

06:18.420 --> 06:20.660
You've been Scouts a long time!

06:20.660 --> 06:22.030
Man, you're annoying!

06:22.030 --> 06:26.030
Are you suggesting the commander
and the captain don't trust us?!

06:26.030 --> 06:29.700
N-No, but that's what
this means, doesn't it?!

06:29.700 --> 06:31.900
Petra! Knock out his teeth!

06:31.900 --> 06:33.700
Switch his front teeth with his back ones!

06:33.700 --> 06:36.540
No, Eren's right.

06:36.540 --> 06:41.880
The captain must've had a
reason for not trusting us implicitly.

06:41.880 --> 06:43.080
Like what?

06:43.080 --> 06:46.580
There's only one reason
he couldn't trust his comrades.

06:46.580 --> 06:49.690
There's someone in the regiment
who can either turn into a Titan

06:49.690 --> 06:53.380
or is working as a sort of spy for them.

06:54.190 --> 06:58.290
You think so too, right?
That there's someone in the regiment...

06:58.290 --> 07:01.790
Mm. I think there is.

07:06.240 --> 07:07.900
A spy?

07:07.900 --> 07:09.810
Are you really sure?

07:09.810 --> 07:13.410
At the very least,
the commander must believe so.

07:13.410 --> 07:16.480
I assume the only soldiers
informed of this operation

07:16.480 --> 07:18.820
were the ones who survived five years ago.

07:18.820 --> 07:19.950
I see.

07:19.950 --> 07:21.320
So that's why...

07:21.320 --> 07:23.420
Yep, that's gotta be it.

07:23.420 --> 07:25.920
Get it, Eren?
That's what's goin' on.

07:25.920 --> 07:28.560
Mm. In that case, it couldn't be helped.

07:28.560 --> 07:29.830
Yeah...

07:29.830 --> 07:33.630
Five years ago
was when the wall first fell...

07:33.630 --> 07:36.100
Could they be using that
fact to narrow down suspects

07:36.100 --> 07:38.940
on the assumption
that's when the spy got inside?

07:38.940 --> 07:42.960
Does that mean this person
killed Sawney and Beane too?

07:43.840 --> 07:48.800
The commander asked me
something after that happened...

07:50.510 --> 07:52.980
What do you see here?

07:52.980 --> 07:55.490
What do you think the enemy is?

07:55.490 --> 07:57.950
Is that what that meant?

07:57.950 --> 08:00.260
We might've been allowed
to join the operation

08:00.260 --> 08:03.860
if we'd known the answer to that question.

08:03.860 --> 08:05.960
I doubt any of us could have, though.

08:05.960 --> 08:08.130
Well, I knew.

08:08.130 --> 08:14.200
But I decided not to say anything.
Do you guys know why?

08:14.200 --> 08:16.010
Why?

08:16.010 --> 08:18.640
What, you mean you don't know?

08:18.640 --> 08:21.610
I guess guys like
you wouldn't know, huh?

08:21.610 --> 08:25.010
You're nowhere near my
level yet, after all.

08:25.010 --> 08:28.450
Seriously, are you still
trying to imitate Captain Levi?

08:28.450 --> 08:30.150
He doesn't talk like that.

08:30.150 --> 08:35.160
If this succeeds, we might actually
learn the truth about this world.

08:35.160 --> 08:39.230
Still, even for that...

08:39.230 --> 08:42.320
...way too many people have died.

08:45.870 --> 08:48.560
Do you think the commander
was wrong to do this?

08:52.180 --> 08:54.240
He wasn't in the right,
I'll tell you that.

08:54.240 --> 08:58.480
If we'd actually been told
that a Titan had inside info,

08:58.480 --> 09:00.850
we would've handled things differently.

09:00.850 --> 09:03.840
Your own squad members, for example...

09:07.820 --> 09:10.930
- No, it wasn't wrong.
- Huh?

09:10.930 --> 09:12.830
How can you say that?

09:12.830 --> 09:16.200
Do you know how many
soldiers have needlessly died?!

09:16.200 --> 09:17.430
Jean.

09:17.430 --> 09:20.740
In hindsight, it's easy to
say what should've been done.

09:20.740 --> 09:22.510
But...

09:22.510 --> 09:24.940
No one can tell how things will turn out.

09:24.940 --> 09:29.280
Yet, at some point
you have to make a choice.

09:30.250 --> 09:32.520
The lives of a hundred comrades...

09:32.520 --> 09:35.420
...or the lives of
everyone inside the walls.

09:35.420 --> 09:37.550
The commander chose.

09:37.550 --> 09:41.790
He chose to throw away
the lives of a hundred comrades.

09:41.790 --> 09:43.060
Eren.

09:43.060 --> 09:47.030
If you didn't know already,
you'll soon learn why

09:47.030 --> 09:53.570
Erwin Smith was put in charge
of the Scouts, of humanity's hope...

09:53.570 --> 09:56.610
It's why he even
has Captain Levi's trust!

09:56.610 --> 10:00.440
That's assuming you
survive long enough, of course.

10:01.310 --> 10:03.910
I don't have much
life experience yet...

10:03.910 --> 10:06.380
...but I do know one thing.

10:06.380 --> 10:09.620
If there's anyone who
can bring about change,

10:09.620 --> 10:14.460
it's someone capable of
giving up what matters most.

10:14.460 --> 10:18.260
In particular, people who are capable
of abandoning their humanity

10:18.260 --> 10:21.900
when forced to rise above monsters.

10:21.900 --> 10:24.730
Those who can't abandon anything...

10:24.730 --> 10:27.600
...can't change anything.

10:40.000 --> 10:41.970
Fire!

10:45.780 --> 10:47.310
How do you like that?

10:47.310 --> 10:51.450
Now you can't scratch a
single itch or move a single muscle.

10:51.450 --> 10:54.350
And you probably never will again.

10:54.350 --> 11:00.620
The more your wounds heal,
the stiffer your joints will get!

11:02.660 --> 11:06.360
Still, why haven't they
extracted our esteemed guest yet?

11:06.360 --> 11:10.230
What are Levi and Miche doing?!

11:34.420 --> 11:40.000
So she has the ability to cover portions
of her body with hardened skin...

11:40.000 --> 11:44.830
Much like the Armored Titan I've heard about.

11:44.830 --> 11:50.210
Will it weaken if we continue
an ODM sword assault?

11:50.210 --> 11:52.110
There's no time to try.

11:52.110 --> 11:53.940
In which case...

11:55.010 --> 11:56.050
Sir!

11:56.050 --> 11:58.010
Prepare to blast it.

11:58.010 --> 11:59.780
Blow off the target's hands.

11:59.780 --> 12:01.080
Yes, Sir!

12:01.080 --> 12:04.090
However, there's a
risk our standard artillery

12:04.090 --> 12:07.620
could take out everything
on the inside as well.

12:07.620 --> 12:12.460
Then let's attempt to
sever the wrists instead.

12:12.460 --> 12:14.760
Fire an all-out salvo on my signal.

12:14.760 --> 12:16.390
Understood!

12:25.240 --> 12:29.480
Hey. Just come out already, will you?

12:29.480 --> 12:32.880
We don't got time for this.

12:32.880 --> 12:36.820
Say, what do you think's
gonna happen to you now?

12:36.820 --> 12:42.220
Do you really think you
can get out of this situation?

12:42.220 --> 12:46.630
I wish you'd pay some thought
to the trouble you've caused us.

12:46.630 --> 12:51.300
You killed our men in
all sorts of different ways.

12:51.300 --> 12:53.960
Was it fun?

12:54.900 --> 12:57.010
Well, I'm having fun now.

12:57.010 --> 13:00.910
I take it you're the same way.

13:00.910 --> 13:05.850
If there's anyone who
knows how I feel, it's you.

13:06.650 --> 13:08.280
Oh, right.

13:08.280 --> 13:11.280
There's one thing I need to ask.

13:11.690 --> 13:15.490
Will you be fine if
your limbs get cut off?

13:15.490 --> 13:17.960
They'll go grow back, right?

13:17.960 --> 13:21.200
I'm talking about your actual body.

13:21.200 --> 13:25.630
Can't afford to have
you die on us, after all...

13:56.530 --> 14:00.530
Damn. You startled me there.

14:01.640 --> 14:04.000
Were those her death throes?

14:06.880 --> 14:08.640
Erwin. I smell them.

14:08.640 --> 14:09.850
Which direction?

14:09.850 --> 14:12.810
All directions, all at once!
Lots of them!

14:17.250 --> 14:20.690
What the?!
They're rushing into the forest all at once!

14:20.690 --> 14:23.020
Why are they suddenly ignoring us?!

14:27.100 --> 14:28.530
What?!

14:28.530 --> 14:31.400
Does this mean they're all Abnormals?!

14:31.400 --> 14:34.200
Doesn't matter! Don't let 'em through!

14:34.200 --> 14:36.330
Commence combat!

14:38.410 --> 14:40.210
What was that all of a sudden?!

14:40.210 --> 14:42.040
Please, wait!

14:42.950 --> 14:45.850
I've heard screams like that before!

14:45.850 --> 14:47.880
In the forest where I'm from!

14:47.880 --> 14:51.620
It's the sound a cornered animal makes
when it's ready to give up everything!

14:51.620 --> 14:55.960
I was taught the end of a hunt
is when you have to be most careful!

14:55.960 --> 14:58.030
So you want me to be careful?

14:58.030 --> 15:00.300
Please be a hundred times
more careful than normal!

15:00.300 --> 15:02.900
You will die if you
don't take the forest seriously!

15:02.900 --> 15:05.400
I'm from the mountains too, actually...

15:05.400 --> 15:08.040
You're a vegetable farmer!
You wouldn't understand!

15:08.040 --> 15:09.440
I see.

15:10.040 --> 15:13.310
Sasha's hunches are often right.

15:13.310 --> 15:17.380
And it's usually only before
something bad happens...

15:17.380 --> 15:22.040
Armin said Eren might be in the
rear of the center rank, as I recall...

15:27.420 --> 15:29.930
Hurry with artillery!

15:29.930 --> 15:30.930
Erwin!

15:30.930 --> 15:34.120
The first wave is coming
from the east! They're close!

15:35.300 --> 15:38.160
Wagon defense squad! Intercept them!

15:44.410 --> 15:47.480
They're ignoring us?!
Are they Abnormals?!

15:47.480 --> 15:49.310
Three Titans have broken through!

15:50.080 --> 15:51.450
Captain Levi!

15:51.450 --> 15:53.150
Hey, you...

15:53.150 --> 15:56.080
You just did something, didn't you?

16:06.260 --> 16:08.920
It went for the female one?

16:10.830 --> 16:14.170
Titans coming from all directions!

16:14.170 --> 16:16.640
All soldiers, commence combat!

16:16.640 --> 16:19.440
Defend the Female Titan at all costs!

16:35.020 --> 16:36.460
No!

16:49.710 --> 16:52.470
All soldiers, withdraw!

16:53.410 --> 16:55.640
Redeploy the formation!

16:56.310 --> 16:58.710
Return to Calaneth District!

17:16.770 --> 17:18.730
We've been bested.

17:19.540 --> 17:23.440
What's with that pathetic look of yours?

17:23.440 --> 17:29.550
This goes to show that the enemy
was prepared to throw away everything.

17:29.550 --> 17:33.120
I never imagined our target
would resort to Titan cannibalization

17:33.120 --> 17:35.680
to dispose of information...

17:36.920 --> 17:41.060
After all that blustering we did
in the courtroom, this is how it turns out...

17:41.060 --> 17:43.130
If we waltz back there now,

17:43.130 --> 17:45.760
who knows what'll happen to Eren or us...

17:45.760 --> 17:48.200
We can think about that once we've returned.

17:48.200 --> 17:52.940
For now, we need to focus on returning
without sustaining any further losses.

17:52.940 --> 17:54.370
For now.

17:55.970 --> 17:58.570
The steam is impairing visibility.

17:58.570 --> 18:02.100
It could hinder smoke signal communications.

18:07.150 --> 18:09.420
I'm going to get my squad.

18:09.420 --> 18:11.250
Wait, Levi.

18:11.450 --> 18:13.490
Replenish your gas and blades first.

18:13.490 --> 18:16.830
We're low on time and
I have enough to last already.

18:16.830 --> 18:18.060
Why?

18:18.060 --> 18:21.800
That's an order. Do as you're told.

18:21.800 --> 18:23.790
Whatever you say, Erwin.

18:24.930 --> 18:27.600
I'll trust your judgment.

18:40.620 --> 18:42.180
The withdrawal signal.

18:42.180 --> 18:45.490
We're all to withdraw and
return to base on horseback.

18:45.490 --> 18:46.790
Right!

18:46.790 --> 18:50.020
What? Is it all over?

18:52.530 --> 18:55.800
All right! We can go home!

18:55.800 --> 18:58.130
Just what's going on?

18:58.130 --> 19:00.120
Is Eren all right?

19:00.800 --> 19:03.210
Looks like it's over.

19:03.210 --> 19:05.940
Let's get back to the
horses! Prepare to withdraw!

19:05.940 --> 19:07.040
You heard the man.

19:07.040 --> 19:12.170
Let's go see what the
bastard riding inside it looks like.

19:13.850 --> 19:16.190
Did they really find out who it is?

19:16.190 --> 19:18.220
All thanks to you!

19:18.220 --> 19:20.020
Huh? But I didn't do anything.

19:20.020 --> 19:22.690
You trusted us, remember?

19:22.690 --> 19:26.830
Things turned out this way
because you chose to stick with us.

19:26.830 --> 19:31.060
Making the right call is a pretty
hard thing to do, you know!

19:31.400 --> 19:34.840
Hey, now. Quit pamperin' him, Petra.

19:34.840 --> 19:36.970
How was he any help?

19:36.970 --> 19:40.480
All he did was whine
like a pathetic little brat.

19:40.480 --> 19:43.880
I guess making it back alive might
be considered praiseworthy,

19:43.880 --> 19:47.850
but only after the
mission's done and over with.

19:47.850 --> 19:52.250
Just so you know, twerp, an expedition
ain't over 'til you're back home.

19:52.250 --> 19:55.350
Yes, I get it already!

19:57.190 --> 19:58.690
Oruo! Petra!

19:58.690 --> 20:02.160
For a couple of soldiers who cried and
pissed their pants during their first battle,

20:02.160 --> 20:04.030
you've really grown!

20:05.070 --> 20:06.200
Don't mention that!

20:06.200 --> 20:08.700
Are you trying to make
him lose respect for me, Eld?!

20:08.700 --> 20:10.210
Whoa, she really did?!

20:10.210 --> 20:11.440
It's the truth.

20:11.440 --> 20:14.010
And, just so you know,
I never pissed myself, Eren.

20:14.010 --> 20:17.750
You idiot! I'll have you know
I have the highest kill count!

20:17.750 --> 20:19.280
I'm the best, you moron!

20:19.280 --> 20:22.120
There's more to a soldier's
merits than just kill counts!

20:22.120 --> 20:23.920
Shut up, you idiot!

20:23.920 --> 20:26.620
Ms. Petra! Does that mean
it sprayed everywhere in midair?!

20:26.620 --> 20:28.020
Knock it off!

20:28.020 --> 20:29.730
Are you on a picnic or something?!

20:29.730 --> 20:31.690
We're outside the walls, you know!

20:31.690 --> 20:34.720
Also, I never wet myself either, Eren!

20:44.410 --> 20:48.080
Oh. That must be a
message from Captain Levi.

20:48.080 --> 20:51.910
We're rendezvousing with the captain!
Stow the chatter until we're home!

21:12.500 --> 21:13.800
Erwin.

21:13.800 --> 21:15.740
Why did you have
Levi replenish his supplies

21:15.740 --> 21:17.610
when there's no time to waste?

21:17.610 --> 21:19.580
The female was eaten.

21:19.580 --> 21:23.150
But did you see the
person inside get eaten?

21:23.150 --> 21:24.580
I didn't.

21:25.280 --> 21:26.320
Are you saying?!

21:26.320 --> 21:27.350
Yes.

21:27.350 --> 21:29.950
If, as you deduced earlier,

21:29.950 --> 21:34.620
we're dealing with a type that remains
able-bodied after de-transformation...

21:34.990 --> 21:39.620
And, if said person had equipped
themselves with ODM gear in advance...

21:40.700 --> 21:45.790
...that means they're now
wearing one of our uniforms...

21:46.370 --> 21:47.860
Captain Levi?

21:48.800 --> 21:50.510
No... It's not!

21:50.510 --> 21:52.000
Who are you?!

22:00.280 --> 22:01.720
M-Mr. Gunther!

22:01.720 --> 22:03.340
Hey! Why?!

22:04.320 --> 22:05.720
Mr. Gunther!

22:14.060 --> 22:18.690
...and have blended in
with the rest of us soldiers.

22:36.200 --> 22:41.590
If we suppose that I am not me,

22:41.590 --> 22:46.130
Can you say with certainty that you are you?

22:46.780 --> 22:51.660
Will you be able to pick up after yourself

22:51.660 --> 22:56.810
Once your sand-like shell breaks and your heart crumbles?

22:57.090 --> 23:02.020
I could hear someone calling

23:02.310 --> 23:05.920
But now my ears are just ringing

23:06.240 --> 23:11.080
It's as if time has frozen

23:11.380 --> 23:13.990
Now, wake up

23:13.990 --> 23:18.960
I began to walk through a deep dark abyss

23:19.510 --> 23:24.260
As swift as a gale, I escaped for my life

23:24.670 --> 23:28.830
I felt like a living corpse

23:29.240 --> 23:33.960
We break out of our walls

23:34.270 --> 23:40.350
To reunite in worlds we've yet to map

23:53.377 --> 23:55.488
The capture operation failed.

23:56.088 --> 23:59.333
The Female Titan appears before Eren once more.

23:59.822 --> 24:03.800
The ones barring its path are a group of Titan-slaying experts

24:04.339 --> 24:06.000
Crushing Blow: The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 5
known as the special-ops squad.

24:06.000 --> 24:07.010
Crushing Blow: The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 5
